     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. Typical prescription doses are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It may be a typo, for example 1600 mg per day in total, or 400 mg four times daily.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office. An order like this should come from, or be verified by, the treating clinician. It shouldn't be entered on a non-clinician's request.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order. If they confirm a corrected dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth up to four times daily, send it to me and I can enter it. If they intentionally want the higher dose, they should enter it themselves and add a note explaining why."
      }
     ],
