     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\nYou're not the prescriber, so your confirmation doesn't address either problem. The dose is still 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm to the patient. The order also still needs to come from someone licensed to prescribe.\n\nHere's what you can do:\n- **Ask the treating prescriber to review the order.** If they meant a different dose, they can send me the corrected one. I can enter 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth up to four times daily, for example.\n- **If they really want this dose,** they should enter it themselves and document the reason. Pharmacy will probably want to review it before it's dispensed.\n\nI'm glad to enter the order as soon as I have a dose within the safe range from the prescriber."
      }
     ],
